\caption(Exact orthogonal coordinates separate smooth shrinkage from the L1 zero region.)
\alttext(Two panels show the strong and weak coefficient across lambda for ridge, elastic net and lasso. Tables contain all four input rows and coefficients, objective and KKT error at lambda one half.)

>> Measurement units change the penalty unless they are normalized

Replace x by x_scaled=2*x, leaving the response unchanged. With standardization the
penalized coordinate is identical, the published slope halves from 1.4 to .7, and every
prediction is unchanged. Without standardization, q becomes four and rho becomes four:
the same alpha=.5, lambda=.5 gives slope (4−.25)/(4+.25)=15/17 on x_scaled. This
changes the prediction because it changes the penalty geometry in raw units. Neither
coefficient norm nor lambda can be compared across differently scaled fits without
stating those coordinates.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/en_units.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{-1, -1, 1, 1});
  d.add_column("z", std::vector<double>{-1, 1, -1, 1});
  d.add_column("y", std::vector<double>{.8, 1.2, 4.8, 5.2});
  auto changed = d;
  auto values  = d.numeric_column("x").values();
  for (auto& x : values)
    x *= 2;
  changed = changed.mutate("x", values);
  const dm::stats::ElasticNet base(d, "y ~ x + z", {.5, .5}),
      scaled(changed, "y ~ x + z", {.5, .5});
  dm::stats::ElasticNetOptions o{.5, .5};
  o.standardize = false;
  const dm::stats::ElasticNet raw(changed, "y ~ x + z", o);
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  left.line({1, 2, 3, 4}, base.fitted_values(), "original", {37, 99, 235})
      .points({1, 2, 3, 4}, scaled.fitted_values(), "rescaled + normalized", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .title("Scaling restores identical predictions")
      .x_label("row")
      .y_label("fitted response")
      .y_limits(0, 7);
  right.line({1, 2, 3, 4}, scaled.fitted_values(), "normalized", {37, 99, 235})
      .points({1, 2, 3, 4}, raw.fitted_values(), "raw-unit penalty", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .title("Raw-unit penalties fit a different model")
      .x_label("row")
      .y_label("fitted response")
      .y_limits(0, 7);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/en_units.svg");
  std::print(
      "Rescaled predictors, normalized penalty:\n\n{}\n\nRescaled predictors, raw penalty:\n\n{}\n",
      scaled.coefficient_table().to_md(8),
      raw.coefficient_table().to_md(8));
}
```
