> Checking the theory

>> Duplicated predictors expose grouping and nonuniqueness

Let x=z and y=2*x, with x=(-1,-1,1,1), lambda=1. Any lasso solution with nonnegative
slopes summing to one is optimal. Cyclic order can put all weight on the first column;
reversing the columns changes the reported allocation but not predictions. With
alpha=.5, strict convexity and exchange symmetry force equal slopes. Substituting
b_x=b_z=b gives 2−2*b=.5+.5*b, hence b=.6. Ridge gives 2/3 on each duplicate.

The table also caps the mixed model at different sweep budgets. A small coefficient
change is checked together with subgradient stationarity, rather than treating any
returned vector as an optimized model. The plot floors KKT errors at 1e-14 only for
logarithmic display; the table retains scientific notation and actual convergence flags.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/en_grouping.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
  d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{-1, -1, 1, 1});
  d.add_column("z", std::vector<double>{-1, -1, 1, 1});
  d.add_column("y", std::vector<double>{-2, -2, 2, 2});
  auto left = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors = {{37, 99, 235}, {22, 163, 74}, {220, 38, 38}};
  const std::vector<std::string>       labels = {"ridge", "elastic net", "lasso"};
  std::size_t                          index  = 0;
  for (double alpha : {0., .5, 1.}) {
    dm::stats::ElasticNetOptions o{alpha, 1};
    o.tol = 1e-12;
    const dm::stats::ElasticNet m(d, "y ~ x + z", o);
    const double                offset = (double(index) - 1) * .25;
    left.bars({1 + offset, 2 + offset}, m.coefficients(), labels[index], colors[index], .22);
    ++index;
  }
  std::vector<double>    budget, errors;
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame table;
  for (std::size_t steps : {1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
    dm::stats::ElasticNetOptions o{.5, 1};
    o.max_iter = steps;
    o.tol      = 1e-12;
    const dm::stats::ElasticNet m(d, "y ~ x + z", o);
    auto                        row =
        m.diagnostics().select({"iterations", "converged", "max_kkt_violation", "objective"});
    row.add_column("budget", std::vector<double>{double(steps)});
    row.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{m.coefficients()[0]});
    row.add_column("z", std::vector<double>{m.coefficients()[1]});
    table = table.ncols() ? table.concat_rows(row) : row;
    budget.push_back(std::log2(steps));
    errors.push_back(
        std::log10(std::max(1e-14, m.diagnostics().double_at("max_kkt_violation", 0))));
  }
  left.title("Identical predictors, different allocations")
      .x_label("column (x=1, z=2)")
      .y_label("coefficient")
      .y_limits(0, 1.6);
  right.line(budget, errors, "KKT residual", {37, 99, 235})
      .points(budget, errors, "", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .title("Stationarity improves across sweeps")
      .x_label("log2 allowed sweep budget")
      .y_label("log10 KKT violation, floor -14")
      .y_limits(-14, 1);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/en_grouping.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits     = 9;
  fmt.scientific = {"max_kkt_violation"};
  std::print("{}\n", table.to_md(fmt));
}
```
