> Iris: paths and a declared held-out comparison

Iris has 150 flowers, four numeric measurements in centimetres and a species label.
Predict Petal.Length from Sepal.Length, Sepal.Width, Petal.Width and the
Sepal.Length:Petal.Width interaction. Species is excluded. The interaction shares
information with its component measurements but does not guarantee a particular
correlation in every dataset.

Before fitting, reserve rows whose zero-based index is divisible by five: 120 training
and 30 test rows, spanning the three species blocks. Training CV uses seed 42 and five
folds. Alpha=.5 is the declared primary model. The table prints the first training
rows, raw/penalized coefficients, selected-lambda diagnostics and the best few grid
candidates. The two plots show the full path and every CV candidate, including any
boundary or unfinished fit; neither plot silently trims errors.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/en_iris_path.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto               d = dm::datasets::iris();
  std::vector<std::size_t> train_rows, test_rows;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < d.nrows(); ++i)
    (i % 5 == 0 ? test_rows : train_rows).push_back(i);
  const auto        train = d.take_rows(train_rows), test = d.take_rows(test_rows);
  const std::string formula =
      "Petal.Length ~ Sepal.Length + Sepal.Width + Petal.Width + Sepal.Length:Petal.Width";
  dm::stats::ElasticNetOptions o;
  o.alpha            = .5;
  o.n_lambda         = 60;
  o.max_iter         = 50000;
  o.tol              = 1e-8;
  o.lambda_min_ratio = 1e-6;
  const dm::stats::ElasticNet m(train, formula, o);
  auto                        left = m.plot_coefficient_path(), right = m.plot_cv_curve();
  left.title("Iris training coefficient path")
      .legend(
          {"SL", "SW", "PW", "SL:PW"}, {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}, {217, 119, 6}})
      .y_limits(-2, 4.5);
  right.title("Five-fold error, all candidates")
      .legend({"CV MSE", "selected"}, {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}})
      .y_limits(0, 4.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(left).add(right).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/en_iris_path.svg");
  dm::dstruct::DataFrame::MarkdownOptions fmt;
  fmt.digits         = 8;
  fmt.scientific     = {"max_kkt_violation"};
  const auto path_ok = m.path_diagnostics().numeric_column("converged").values(),
             fold_ok = m.cv_fold_results().numeric_column("converged").values();
  std::print(
      "{} training and {} reserved test rows.\nConverged path fits: {}/{}; converged fold fits: "
      "{}/{}.\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\nBest grid candidates:\n\n{}\n",
      train.nrows(),
      test.nrows(),
      std::count(path_ok.begin(), path_ok.end(), 1),
      path_ok.size(),
      std::count(fold_ok.begin(), fold_ok.end(), 1),
      fold_ok.size(),
      train.head(3).to_md(2),
      m.coefficient_table().to_md(8),
      m.diagnostics()
          .select({"alpha", "lambda", "iterations", "converged", "max_kkt_violation", "objective"})
          .to_md(fmt),
      m.path_diagnostics().sort_by("cv_mse", true).head(5).to_md(fmt));
}
```
